cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the SurfTracker pipeline in scientific work, please cite BOTH
  primary articles listed in references: Shi et al. (2008) for cortical
  sulcus/gyrus segmentation and Hamilton-Jacobi skeletons, and Nie et al.
  (2024) for surface-based probabilistic superficial white matter tracking.
  Please also report the software version and processing settings used.
type: software
title: "SurfTracker: superficial white matter surface tracking"
authors:
  - family-names: Nie
    given-names: Xinyu
  - family-names: Shi
    given-names: Yonggang
